From 38a7ada8cc2d73549b69e9739227e0f901299ef3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mario Maalini <magalinimario@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:46:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add opt-in reputation observation channel

Each agent's reputation rep_i = R_i - mean_{j!=i} R_j, with
R_i(t) = lambda * R_i(t-1) + r_i(t), is appended to the observation as one
extra channel holding rep_j at agent j's cell in each agent's egocentric view.

- Envs report info["individual_rewards"] (per-agent reward before any
  common/shaped conversion) in every reward mode.
- socialjax/wrappers/reputation.py: ReputationWrapper (R resets per episode).
- socialjax.make(..., reputation=True, reputation_lambda=...) applies it.
- REPUTATION / REPUTATION_LAMBDA in every *_base.yaml; train.py forwards them
  to ENV_KWARGS so it works for all algorithms (default off).
- tests/test_reputation.py: formula, reset, shapes, and view alignment
  against each env's own obs for all 8 grid envs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
